			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Replace Echo emoji from ⚡ to 📣 across README.md\n\nUpdate the emoji icon for the Echo work-stealing scheduler component from ⚡ (lightning bolt) to 📣 (megaphone) in four locations across the README.md: the Overview section describing Mountain's architecture, the component Dependency table, the Crate Dependencies table, and the Compatibility section.\n\nThe lightning bolt emoji was visually ambiguous when rendered alongside other monochrome emoji and could suggest electrical/hardware concerns rather than task coordination. The megaphone emoji better conveys Echo's role as a work-stealing notification and dispatch scheduler. All references now use consistent iconography aligned with Echo's actual architectural purpose.",
			"SHA": "dddba51efa7e796b2cd4543c2d545a2a17cd08d7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-07-08T16:27:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1910,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Expand funding acknowledgements with table header and description\n\nAdd a persuasive narrative paragraph introducing the Land project and its funding partners to the Funding & Acknowledgements section, replacing the sparse existing text. Add a proper thead row labeling each funding/partner entity (Land, PlayForm, NLnet, NGI0 Commons Fund) above the logo table, improving scannability and semantic structure. Normalize the Land logo link from mixed-case to lowercase domain `editor.land`, and adjust the Changelog section copy to remove the parenthetical \"Mountain\"-specific qualifier and add a welcoming lead-in phrase.\n\nProse now better communicates the project's open-source mission to casual readers, and the structured table header makes the sponsorship hierarchy immediately visible at a glance.",
			"SHA": "ce6045a00e1f2657a92e2703f151e2d6b7626f7c"
		}
	],
